WEBVTT

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:08.830
This past Saturday, we lost a television legend and our friend, Bob Barker.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:14.560
Bob was an amazing man who set the gold standard not only for his performance on camera,

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:19.510
but for his off-camera love and support of all animals big and small.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.780
Most people remember Bob from the 35 years he spent hosting The Price is Right.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:30.000
So it's easy to forget that for 18 years, he was a fixture in America's living rooms for Truth or Confidence.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.180
A radio host before that, and a naval aviator during World War II.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:39.810
We'll also remember Bob for his tireless work on behalf of all animals,

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:45.010
from whales and elephants to the cats and dogs he reminded everybody at the end of the show to get spayed or neutered.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:52.040
You know, I mentioned the word legend earlier, and while that word gets thrown around all too much these days,

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:56.960
it couldn't be more appropriate when you think about Bob's time on The Price is Right.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.000
Bob's skills were second nature to him.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.910
He was the master of the game.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:05.220
But he always knew who the real stars of his show were--

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.840
the contestants.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.190
Today, we celebrate Bob's legacy with a look back

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:13.170
at some of the incredible moments of his time here

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.260
on "The Price is Right."

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.290
This is for you, Bob.

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:21.220
The star of the new "Price is Right."

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:45.060
Oh my goodness, he's Bob-a-licious.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:52.790
I want you to remember at home that I'm Bob-a-licious.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:56.980
Well, okay.

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:46.550
I got you, so I had to come down here.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.860
What were we doing in the dream?

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.460
You were chasing me in the hayloft.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:54.140
One, two, three, open it.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.630
There's a moment you're in the back.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:06.830
Thank you very much.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:08.660
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:11.300
And I want to thank you folks there at home.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:13.990
And I want to thank you, too, for what you say

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:16.930
when I'm the guy who gives away all the refrigerators.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:21.270
I thank you for watching The Price is Right so consistently

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:25.130
that we are still the highest-rated game show in television.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:30.000
Mike Green has a little...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:36.910
boy was to pitch for the St. Louis Cardinals, but I didn't because of a total lack of talent.

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:41.910
Well I got my job, my first job in radio, when I was still in college. My wife and I

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:46.330
had been married. I'd been a naval aviator, and when I got my wings, we got married. I

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:53.140
wrote local news and I did a sportscast. But finally, I did what I'm doing right now. I

00:03:53.140 --> 00:04:00.000
did an audience participation show. And my wife heard that. She said, "Barker, that's

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.830
You did that better than you ever done anything else.

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:05.380
She didn't say I was good.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:08.660
She said I did it better than I'd ever done anything else.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:10.940
One of the most fortunate things in my life

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:14.590
was the fact that Ralph Edwards came into my life.

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:16.530
He had sold "Truth or Consequences"

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:19.410
as a daytime show on NBC.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:24.030
He heard me doing my audience participation radio show.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.270
He liked my work, called me, and that he would like

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:30.000
to talk about me becoming the host.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:34.240
He said, "When would it be convenient for you to meet with me?"

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.900
I said, "Mr. Edwards, I can be over there in 15 minutes.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.000
I'm on my way."

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.260
Remember this name.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.680
You're going to be hearing a lot about him.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:45.290
Here he is, ladies and gentlemen, Mr. Bob Barker.

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:52.270
And then on December 21, 1956, at 5 minutes past 12:00 noon,

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:54.770
Ralph Edwards called me, and he told me

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:57.700
that I was to be the host of "Truth or Consequences."

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.080
Hiya, kid, limber.

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:00.000
All set.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.840
Let's see.

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:02.260
Yep, yep, he's ready, relax.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:04.530
- We did "Truth or Consequences" live.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:08.430
We did it first from the NBC studio at Sunset and Vine,

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:11.530
and then we did it at the old El Capitan Theater.

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:15.230
Eventually, we were one of the first shows to go to color,

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:17.230
at which time we went out to Burbank.

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:19.030
- Well, until next time, this is Bob Barker saying,

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:20.540
"Why don't I get more money?"

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:23.330
Goodbye, everybody.

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:27.240
- Mark Goodson had seen me on "Truth or Consequences,"

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:28.830
and he liked my work.

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:30.000
This was to be a network.

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:31.750
"The Price is Right."

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.840
And he told me he'd like to have me hosted.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:38.080
I met with him, and he told me what he had planned.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:40.920
And he said, what do you think, Bob?

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:42.710
And I said, I think it'll work.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.410
He said, I do too.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.110
I think we'll get a long run out of this.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:51.480
"The Price is Right" actually started over 65 years ago,

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:54.810
back in 1956, then went off the air for a few years,

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:57.460
and then was brought back as the new "Price is Right"

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:00.000
on September 4, 1972, by CBS.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.410
Now, if you've ever seen the original show that was hosted by another TV legend, Bill

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:10.050
Cullen, you know that this new Price is Right was quite a bit different from what viewers

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:11.300
were used to.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:15.530
So it was no small task when Bob went on the air for the first time to let America know

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:17.550
what they were in for.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:23.430
Charming, charismatic, and in complete control, here's Bob on the very first episode of the

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:27.330
new Price is Right.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:30.000
New Price is Right, show number 101-109.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.600
Come on down, you're the first contestant on "The New Price is Right"!

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:45.020
-The star of "The New Price is Right"! -Thank you so much.

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:53.630
Welcome to "The New Price is Right" and let me assure you fans of "The Old Price is Right"

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:57.920
that this is your favorite game still based on the pricing of merchandise

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:00.000
with wonderful things.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.000
wonderful awards for smart shoppers.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.000
We call it the new prices, right, because we

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.000
have some exciting new games that you will enjoy

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.000
right there at home with our studio

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.000
audience, and we're going to get that first game

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.000
going right now. Here's the first

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:16.000
item up for bids, $595,

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.000
and Connie is our winner.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.530
Hello, right here, Connie.

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:23.760
I get the impression you're happy.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.840
Oh, am I? You may win

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.840
this. Yeah, I see it.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.600
It's a power!

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:35.270
What number is next?

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:36.040
Four.

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:36.860
Number four.

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:38.640
Let's see that number four.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:40.880
Number four.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:44.480
One more number and you own the car.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:45.940
One more number, you own the range.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:47.080
What number do you want, Connie?

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:47.840
Six.

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:48.420
Six.

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:49.800
Let's see number six.

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:58.650
You're our top winner of the day.

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:00.000
Paul, you're our runner-up.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:03.550
So you two are going to compete in our showcase round.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:05.290
All right, let's show Connie and Paul

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:07.560
this first showcase, please.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:09.720
It's a trip to Acapulco.

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:13.450
What's your bid?

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:14.270
You'll have to tell me.

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:16.870
- $1,750.

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:18.490
- $1,750.

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:21.930
The actual retail price of your showcase is?

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:24.340
$2,307.

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:26.680
That means that the difference between your bid

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:30.000
and the retail price is?

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:36.120
Paul, you must be closer than that in order to win the car.

00:08:36.470 --> 00:08:37.230
Let's see.

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:41.320
$2,504, Connie.

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:45.080
My only hope is we always have a Connie on The New Price is Right.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:45.500
Thank you very much.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:46.660
Bob Barker, say goodbye.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:47.500
Bye, everybody.

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:57.560
What made Bob uniquely Bob?

00:08:58.260 --> 00:08:59.980
It's actually kind of hard to put a finger on it.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.060
He was hardly flamboyant.

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:03.750
He didn't draw attention to himself.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:06.740
And he was never the cliched game show host.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:08.910
So, you know, what was it?

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:12.390
I think it was the ability to bring out the best in everyone.

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:15.260
He had an innate sixth sense that enabled him to know

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:17.250
when he was going to hit hay dirt.

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:19.650
See for yourself.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.820
Is the eight right?

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:23.140
Of course.

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:26.340
Now, this is an interesting number.

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:30.000
You will recall he had a three up there.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.930
going to leave that. Oh, no. He changed it to five.

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:38.680
Was that a mistake? No. He did the right thing.

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:42.930
He did the right thing. Now, what?

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:43.950
Come on.

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:46.120
You want to hurry it up a little bit.

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:49.180
All right. Is that-- why are you in such a rush?

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:50.370
I'm nervous.

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:51.070
Are you nervous?

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:52.290
Yeah, I'm coming a heart attack.

00:09:52.390 --> 00:09:53.930
Now, you're a young man, and you're in good health,

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:54.620
aren't you?

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:55.320
I think so.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:59.050
Yes, because if you're wrong, I don't want you to become

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:00.000
ill or anything like that.

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:02.050
- I want to sit down.

00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:04.520
- Sit down, go ahead, sit down.

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:06.370
Get in the chair and relax.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.310
There you go, just a moment.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:10.850
Where are you, you're leaving, Cameron.

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:13.120
Get the chair back up here.

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:17.310
Now sit down, Cameron, sit down.

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:19.490
There you go, there you go.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:23.560
All right, Cameron, now, is it a nine?

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:25.810
Yes, Cameron, it's a nine.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:28.550
It's a nine, Cameron, it's a nine.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:33.580
Now, Cameron, if that is a zero, you win--

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:37.080
if it's a zero, you win all these prizes and the car.

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:38.340
Is it a zero?

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:39.240
You're a winner.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.340
You're a winner.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:42.290
Lower.

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:44.590
He says it's lower if he is right.

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:47.630
Of course, he wins the trip to Tahiti.

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:50.290
Is it lower?

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:55.500
Oh, Robert, now you know what I'm worried about.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:56.160
Yes.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:57.440
What?

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:00.000
Do I have a chip next to the crest?

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:01.090
- Shell.

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:02.190
- That's right.

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:03.790
But to be more specific,

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:06.870
what I'm really worried about in as few words as possible

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:08.090
is the ball here.

00:11:08.090 --> 00:11:08.850
- Yes.

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:11.370
I don't think it's there.

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:13.410
- What I'm gonna suggest is we baby up on it.

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:14.760
Let's not look under that one.

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:15.600
- Okay.

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:16.330
- Let's look here.

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:17.170
- Okay.

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:18.010
- We'll think positively.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:18.850
- Definitely.

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:19.930
- If it's here, you win.

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:20.770
- Right.

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:22.360
- You think it's here?

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:25.790
- No.

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:28.470
- You're right, it's not there.

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:29.760
All right now, Robert.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.450
Do you think it's here?

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:34.230
- Yes.

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:37.470
- Oh, now it's really getting serious, Robert.

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:38.910
Now it's here or here.

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:41.160
Which one do you want to look under?

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:42.660
- It's got to be there.

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:43.700
- It has got to be there.

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:45.040
Do you think it'd help if you look

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:46.140
or do you want me to lift it up?

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:47.160
- It'll help if I look.

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:49.100
- Well, all right, then you go ahead and look.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.350
I haven't had any luck.

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:57.390
- You're right, thank you, Robert.

00:11:57.390 --> 00:11:58.560
Congratulations.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:00.000
You'll still have a lot of money.

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:03.870
Well, aren't you interested in figuring these things out?

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:05.870
No, not really.

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:08.140
I've forgotten what you said.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:09.510
Did you say two?

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:11.230
Two, you said two.

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:12.130
He said two.

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:13.630
It's two.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:14.370
There he goes.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:24.230
What do you wish to bid on those surfboards?

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:28.640
$9,000.

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:30.000
$9,000.

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:36.310
Now, before I read this, before I go on,

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:42.270
Isla, I want to see you after the show.

00:12:42.270 --> 00:12:48.170
I have a surfboard I want to give you a good price on.

00:12:48.170 --> 00:12:50.930
If you think a surfboard is $4,500,

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:55.410
I am going to give you the bargain of your life.

00:12:55.410 --> 00:13:00.000
She believes that the price of that automobile is $15,100.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.500
$299.

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:03.400
And, you know, you sound--

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:06.200
You act-- you act as if you really want this car.

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:07.340
I want the car.

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:08.880
You really want this car.

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:10.700
Are you having trouble with the car?

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:11.490
I can't breathe.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:12.900
Can't breathe?

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:14.000
OK, I can breathe.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:15.300
I can breathe.

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:16.300
I'm fine.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:17.630
You all right now?

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:18.660
Yes, I'm fine.

00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:19.860
I'm kind of worried.

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:22.060
No, but if you-- if you lose the car, you'll be all right.

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:23.060
I'll be OK.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:23.860
You'll recover.

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:24.960
Yes.

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:26.240
Very well, let's find out.

00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:27.540
She wins the car.

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:29.600
She wins that car.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.600
A big pull.

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:33.420
There it goes.

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:34.580
Now, what did it start on?

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:37.070
It did not get all the way around.

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:40.300
Now, do you want me to do it for you?

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:41.440
Probably.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:42.580
Would you like to have me do it for you?

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:42.800
Please.

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:43.760
All right, I will.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:45.420
I'll just plain do it for you.

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:48.100
Here we go for Juanita.

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:52.400
She has to beat 75 cents.

00:13:53.070 --> 00:13:56.880
And Juanita, that didn't go all the way around.

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:09.030
After 19 years, that is the most humiliating moment of my life on "Price is Right."

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:09.980
Just a moment.

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:10.980
Just a moment.

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:12.280
I want you to hear something I think you mean.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:13.280
What did you say?

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:15.280
Would you like me to try it again?

00:14:15.280 --> 00:14:19.200
I take back what I said a moment ago.

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:22.520
That is the most humiliating moment of my life.

